#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156994 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157393 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9c799d6-e3fe-5b78-986d-f2068b2db058" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "65957407-b302-51c5-93d9-0f71f3517362" :question/math-academy-id "e-10527" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = 2x, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 1\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\textrm{E}[X] = \\dfrac{2}{3},$ compute $\\textrm{E}[5X^2 - 2X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\textrm{E}[aX + bY] = a\\textrm{E}[X] + b\\textrm{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5{X}^{2}-2X] & =5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[X]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X^n] = \\int_S x^n \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\textrm E [X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\textrm{E}[X] = \\dfrac{2}{3}$ and $\\textrm{E}[X^2] = \\dfrac{1}{2}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5{X}^{2}-2X] & =5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156995 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bada6a7f-c02e-51cd-8ea2-0594a94648a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Second Moment of a Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "292610ec-9c27-590d-b207-c76adc959d55" :question/math-academy-id "e-10528" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n![](images/f3/f3149524cf7975083139c82369095a564c5cb28e66ecd1bdab94721c64bd6d21.svg)\n\nCalculate $\\textrm{E}[X^2].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of $X^2$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X^2] = \\int_{S} x^2 \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of $X^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}+\\frac{3}{8}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}(0+8)+\\frac{3}{8}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156996 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "88bd32d5-4a84-58b3-a3e9-73bf32cb5e4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Higher Moments of a Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "4c5666a4-f477-5b1a-8d17-1e2aa594863f" :question/math-academy-id "e-10529" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n![](images/19/1940f446dbc6c352b86f413501008abd7ac519a79cfa6be9b7207ecfe13609a7.svg)\n\nCalculate $\\textrm E [X^4].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X^n] = \\int_{S} x^n \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fourth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\cdot (1-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}-\\frac{1}{6}\\,{x}^{6})\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{10}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{1}{6}-0)+\\frac{1}{10}(32-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}+\\frac{31}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{47}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157393 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9c799d6-e3fe-5b78-986d-f2068b2db058" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33cb4776-7d73-5e89-be66-3abb80c22cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427291} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5bf664-a18f-566d-a4f7-3bd738b55f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427301} {:answer/id #uuid "74d74ac0-e401-549d-95e1-5b551db31568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427309} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2240d8-61b4-5dec-86e4-1ecedc83ab1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427322} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1156f5-fddd-5d6b-adf1-9732ee27312f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33cb4776-7d73-5e89-be66-3abb80c22cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427291} :answer-field/id #uuid "62e8ebaf-8a75-5cb6-8621-5bcf5f7ac9e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63bcffd8-dbf0-5c48-8ca6-56531c05d1c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-131141" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2x},\\,{e}^{-2}<x<1\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}},$ compute $\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X]=4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[X]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{e}^{-2}}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{e}^{-2}}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\,|}_{{e}^{-2}}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X] & =4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}})-2(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}-1+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157393 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9c799d6-e3fe-5b78-986d-f2068b2db058" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b15167c-cc7e-5c97-9101-4beaf41df4c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427292} {:answer/id #uuid "5871acd5-eca9-59af-9564-3f4745f98b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427299} {:answer/id #uuid "c36cdb5e-f036-5f06-b3d4-eee0c3b0cd8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427328} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2112a6-93fa-5273-9274-f2059365dc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427332} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4b8c9f-2f56-5d9d-9eb5-3c123022c710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca2112a6-93fa-5273-9274-f2059365dc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427332} :answer-field/id #uuid "dea27d55-adba-575a-832b-07b425bd7bd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90065876-8b39-51cd-875c-5aa5721dc0eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-131143" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,0<x<3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5]=2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-5\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=3$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5] & =2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-5 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157393 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9c799d6-e3fe-5b78-986d-f2068b2db058" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ec450b-8c39-502c-a433-fd5a4ae4c4b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427276} {:answer/id #uuid "2fa99956-5688-5c52-8334-d71d3728db7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427290} {:answer/id #uuid "4c69f0cd-2d3b-5d9b-93f3-eb5246d17118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427296} {:answer/id #uuid "6a512d3a-69fb-533d-ab31-f86e2b7a5a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427305} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8387ce-7fb7-5149-8880-aa33c2402f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fa99956-5688-5c52-8334-d71d3728db7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427290} :answer-field/id #uuid "802be14b-ba00-571d-9732-af1b4692f20a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "993709fe-5242-5062-93c5-df6c430c3cdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-131152" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,1<x<2\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ compute $\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}]=2\\text{E}[X]-5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=2$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}] & =2\\text{E}[X]-5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "88bd32d5-4a84-58b3-a3e9-73bf32cb5e4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Higher Moments of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c823865-e861-5d67-a8dd-12a609a5d5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153869} {:answer/id #uuid "c54e1733-eedb-5175-93f7-00f0ff85140d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{75}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153870} {:answer/id #uuid "12aa8baa-a74b-5d99-92f6-b0ee93089a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153871} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8339af-aa00-5d70-912d-8abbe719a9a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153872} {:answer/id #uuid "60e2dd92-ba17-5b89-b3ee-88e17ff1d026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12aa8baa-a74b-5d99-92f6-b0ee93089a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153871} :answer-field/id #uuid "e56bd0b8-dd44-5b86-a00c-3b8ef788a24e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "50e246df-b4af-588d-81cb-30d14deb51ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-149703" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}, & 1<x\\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3{x}^{3}}, & 2\\le x<4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fourth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x\\,{|}_{1}^{2}+{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{2}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =3(2-1)+\\frac{2}{3}(16-4) \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bada6a7f-c02e-51cd-8ea2-0594a94648a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Second Moment of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a13ee3f-d613-5356-b098-bfd4fd31aaad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427295} {:answer/id #uuid "758281e4-a9bd-53f0-8d16-4de28b45b246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427311} {:answer/id #uuid "9c78447b-33fa-5682-bca2-d662339a7e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427320} {:answer/id #uuid "d48438e0-ad44-5549-be39-5c0e85922b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427335} {:answer/id #uuid "e9581c29-d1f3-501f-b511-24d9262ee1fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(e+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d48438e0-ad44-5549-be39-5c0e85922b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427335} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe3f6c56-86fd-5d50-bf8e-6a665c9d1d81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da4e5265-9949-5f02-b346-af79bf8d00ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-152893" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,1\\le x\\le e.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bada6a7f-c02e-51cd-8ea2-0594a94648a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Second Moment of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "473710fd-9ead-5a45-b8c2-95659c60b704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427293} {:answer/id #uuid "86079644-a0ec-53b0-b8f8-e8a0cb61db27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427314} {:answer/id #uuid "88fd42b9-4ac4-58d1-b39c-9aa903c9ce8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427316} {:answer/id #uuid "c62aec32-e023-537a-a5de-f2c36d94cec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427331} {:answer/id #uuid "d0830450-b640-5ef8-acf1-352175173674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0830450-b640-5ef8-acf1-352175173674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427334} :answer-field/id #uuid "7772a622-a1f8-5d76-a766-05c455036ddd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ced0c63-cf37-5cdb-ae0d-645ad331eb6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-152894" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-2{x}^{-1/2})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a}}-1) \\\\  & =-5(0-1) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bada6a7f-c02e-51cd-8ea2-0594a94648a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Second Moment of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1787c976-b394-5db2-9647-7788ad9018da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427281} {:answer/id #uuid "17b6397b-6d8a-502f-b1bb-d6805bac1e89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427282} {:answer/id #uuid "69257811-1577-5b8b-814f-a4ffc4c0084f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427304} {:answer/id #uuid "8386f4fd-561f-5977-a7b8-f5fa721f4d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427313} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5e19b7-9577-599a-b29a-d5fbd4562df7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec5e19b7-9577-599a-b29a-d5fbd4562df7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427341} :answer-field/id #uuid "03eb10c9-9e29-5bb8-8db9-ad1064b9deaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84598522-637e-5d77-b555-f1f4d414ed22" :question/math-academy-id "q-152899" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & -1<x<0, \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\,x, & 0\\le x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(0+1)+\\frac{1}{3}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427372 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bada6a7f-c02e-51cd-8ea2-0594a94648a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Second Moment of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9101a2-c4eb-5ffc-8017-56ef5d0f4631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427280} {:answer/id #uuid "74b705a1-7b7f-567b-b1a0-4e5f5a39eca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427308} {:answer/id #uuid "88154b96-2e73-5a0a-bc21-32bcd5e8f45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427315} {:answer/id #uuid "c59c5886-4339-5c0d-ad4e-c08302875680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427330} {:answer/id #uuid "e30c5074-c231-5111-a50b-ae42316e1152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88154b96-2e73-5a0a-bc21-32bcd5e8f45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427315} :answer-field/id #uuid "a45670cd-9618-5c8d-b9e3-77951bdb7b1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e993c85-9e06-5795-8658-efd529bfafbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-152900" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}\\,{x}^{3}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}\\,{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{7}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bada6a7f-c02e-51cd-8ea2-0594a94648a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Second Moment of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0addfc1b-9d02-54e5-8a6c-dd9cd58986f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427279} {:answer/id #uuid "17fc818e-1be8-57fa-8910-2ceb34d1bfea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427283} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb44b98-48db-57a3-ba4e-4af609be3544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427289} {:answer/id #uuid "70d02cfc-345f-501e-aae7-81b360481a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427306} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0bfc22-7fbd-53d9-bfaf-6dd316f1bf07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17fc818e-1be8-57fa-8910-2ceb34d1bfea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427283} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea5d3c17-6171-5c4e-88bb-85a10dbabe26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10b4599a-65d6-546d-a1db-2b8fd1bfb09d" :question/math-academy-id "q-152901" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}, & -1<x<0, \\\\ {x}^{2}, & 0\\le x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(0+1)+\\frac{1}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{45}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "88bd32d5-4a84-58b3-a3e9-73bf32cb5e4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Higher Moments of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "208a0b10-d20c-5680-b78b-191ae08c910b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427287} {:answer/id #uuid "92ac3001-cb5a-5ac0-aae9-3